WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.730
Encoding changes how software represents a variable
It does not

00:00:05.757 --> 00:00:11.416
change the underlying meaning Nominal variables
often use one-hot

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:17.273
indicators Ordinal variables may use ordered
categorical dtypes or explicit ordinal

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:23.273
codes Numeric variables can remain numeric and may
be scaled for methods that need comparable

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:28.820
feature scales Counts should remain conceptually
counts even if a model

00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:34.737
later transforms them The representation should
support not redefine

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:35.750
the concept
